*.local
*.local.*

# Scratch directory (TMPDIR set via .envrc)
.tmp/*
!.tmp/.gitkeep

# Plugin-generated per-repo state. Claude Code clones this repo onto every
# user's machine when they run `claude plugin marketplace add`, so anything
# tracked here ships to all consumers. A submodule tracked here is worse than
# leakage — it breaks the install outright (see CLAUDE.md, "Why This Repo Is
# Different"). Keep these on disk for local tooling; never commit them.
.punt-labs/
.vox/
.lux/
.biff
.beads/
.claude/agents/

# Same leak, narrower paths — these sit beside files the repo legitimately
# tracks, so they are named individually. Ignoring all of `.claude/` or all of
# `.github/workflows/` would mask real content: `.github/workflows/docs.yml`
# is this repo's only CI.
#   settings.json  — written by `vox enable` and punt-kit init; registers hooks
#                    by absolute path to one machine's plugin install, so it is
#                    inert-to-broken on anyone else's disk.
#   hooks/         — written by punt-kit init; the scripts those hooks invoke.
#   biff-notify.yml — written by `biff enable`; posts session events to the
#                    team's NATS relay, and would run in every consumer's fork
#                    against credentials they do not have.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/hooks/
.github/workflows/biff-notify.yml

# A submodule here does not leak data, it breaks the install: Claude Code
# clones this repo with submodules, so an SSH submodule URL aborts the clone
# for every user without a GitHub SSH key. This entry is a backstop, not the
# enforcement — `git submodule add` stages .gitmodules with --force and it
# lands in the index regardless of this line (verified). What the ignore does
# buy is keeping a leftover .gitmodules out of a routine `git add -A`. The
# leak-guard job in .github/workflows/docs.yml is what actually fails the
# build, and it checks the gitlink (mode 160000) as well as this file.
.gitmodules

# The lux display process writes ImGui window geometry into its working
# directory on exit — Lux.ini, Lux_Display.ini, imgui.ini. Per-machine screen
# state (pane sizes, docking layout) that would follow a consumer's window
# manager around. The pattern is broad because the filename comes from
# whichever lux window wrote it; no .ini is ever marketplace content.
*.ini

# The mandated sibling lock every punt CLI takes before mutating a shared
# host file (tool-enable-disable.md 2.4). Per-machine runtime state, and it
# persists by design — unlinking a lock file races the next writer. The
# pattern is broad because the lock's name is the host file's, and tools
# differ on the suffix — .CLAUDE.md.lock and .CLAUDE.md.punt-import.lock
# both appear.
.*.lock
